<title>USA: National Home Health Q2 net rises.</title>
<headline>National Home Health Q2 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>SCARSDALE, N.Y. 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three Months Ended January 31,</p>
<p>						1997		  1996(a)</p>
<p> Revenues			    $8,692,000	    $9,965,000</p>
<p> Net income			  493,000(b)		 471,000</p>
<p> Avg shares			   5,095,321	  5,002,256(c)</p>
<p> Earnings per share			 .10		     .09</p>
<p>					   Six Months Ended January 31,</p>
<p>						1997		  1996(a)</p>
<p> Revenues			    17,378,000	    20,039,000</p>
<p> Net income			1,031,000(b)		 923,000</p>
<p> Avg shares			   5,095,321	  5,001,708(c)</p>
<p> Earnings per share			 .20		     .18</p>
<p>(a) Includes the results of SunStar Healthcare Inc, a wholly owned subsidiary until May 1996 and, thereafter, 37.6%-owned and accounted for under the equity method.</p>
<p>(b) Includes a net charge of $98,000 in the three months ended January 31 1997 and a net charge of $118,000 in the six months ended January 31 1997 related to a loss from equity investee in SunStar Healthcare Inc. (c) Adjusted for a 6% stock dividend paid in December 1996.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
